I will be doing weekly episode videos for
all 4 DC TV Shows That’s Gotham of course,

00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:36.440
The Flash, Arrow and Constantine, all of the
new ones are great so be sure to subscribe

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.740
to get all that stuff.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.290
I’m probably going to be giving away some
DC Swag throughout the year for each of the

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:42.290
shows.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.880
Here’s my non-spoilery review of Gotham
Episode 1 with some set up on what the show

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.760
looks like compared to all the other movies
and tv show:

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.350
The show is told from Detective Gordon’s
Perspective played by Ben McKenzie.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:54.630
It has all the DNA of the Batman Universe
from the comics without looking like it’s

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.410
straight up trying to copy the Gotham from
the Christopher Nolan movies.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:01.310
The thing about the Christopher Nolan movies
were that they treated the Batman Mythos as

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:04.070
if it were happening in modern day with real
people.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.710
No wacky super powers or anything like that.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.470
Gotham the tv series is a little more open
to the idea of superpowers, even though it’s

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.750
not going straight to Justice League like
Arrow and The Flash.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:18.350
It’s starting out with James Gordon in his
first year on the force, which is where you

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.240
get a lot of the Batman Year One similarities.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:27.850
I didn’t watch Ben McKenzie on Southland,
but the way I thought of it when I was watching

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:34.960
the episode was this is Training Day and McKenzie
is playing the Ethan Hawke character and Donal

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.210
Logue is the Denzel Washington Character.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:42.590
I’m just talking about their relationship
and where Gordon’s character fits in with

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.590
everyone else.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.549
Detective Bullock, played by Donal Logue is
the other shining star of the series of course.

00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:54.340
If you’ve ever seen any of the characters
he’s played on other TV Shows, you totally

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.909
get why he’s perfect for Bullock.

00:01:55.909 --> 00:01:59.869
It’s not the Bullock from Batman the Animated
Series, he’s not that sleazy, yet.

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:00.869
But he’s close.

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:05.450
I know I made the Training Day Denzel reference,
but on the show I think of him as being true

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:08.569
neutral, he’s not straight up dirty but
he’s not the quarterback Jim Gordon is trying

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:09.569
to be.

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:10.569
In the timeline, when Gordon shows up in episode
1, he’s already a detective transferring

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:11.569
in from another city.

00:02:11.569 --> 00:02:12.569
So he’s not a total rookie, but he is a
rookie to Gotham City.

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:16.670
The city itself is just as big a character
as anyone else.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:22.980
I feel like that’s something that’s always
really important in the comics and the show

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.010
deals with that in a good way.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:29.760
And one of the most fun things about the show
is the way it sets up the character arc for

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.760
the city.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.709
Visually it takes a lot from Ridley Scott’s
Blade Runner.

00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:36.639
The difference is that in that movie, it was
Los Angeles of the future and Gotham has always

00:02:36.639 --> 00:02:39.349
been an analog of New York City.

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:42.650
Just like Blade Runner you get the sense that
the city is slowly dying.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:48.870
There’s this belief that Matter only has
two states of existence, growth and decay.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.200
The implication being that if you’re not
evolving, you’re in the process of dying.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:56.129
The City, when we first see it, is already
in a state of Decay.

00:02:56.129 --> 00:03:00.599
The idea is that over the course of the entire
series, the city will turn into a chaos vacuum

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:03.560
that just eats all light and goodness.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:06.769
That’s when Batman puts on the cowl to fill
the vacuum.

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:13.340
I think it was said at some point that where
we start in season 1, Bruce Wayne is about

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.079
8 years from putting the cowl on.

00:03:16.079 --> 00:03:19.279
He’s pre-highschool age.

00:03:19.279 --> 00:03:23.040
Quick Sidenote, there is actually a batman
comic set in gotham city with high school

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.040
kids.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.040
It’s called Gotham Academy.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.709
I recommend you check it out on comixology.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:34.400
The rogues gallery of villains that creates
that vacuum is led by Jada Pinkett Smith as

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.239
the crime boss Fish Mooney and Robin Lord
Taylor as Oswald Cobblepot one of her underlings.

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:43.859
If you’re a walking dead fan, you might
remember him from Season 4.

00:03:43.859 --> 00:03:44.859
He was Sam.

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:47.640
The guy Carol and Rick ran into and almost
killed.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.389
Smith is interesting as a villain.

00:03:49.389 --> 00:03:52.159
I wasn’t really familiar with her character
going into it.

00:03:52.159 --> 00:03:57.200
Because this is a 16 plus episode season,
we’ll see a lot more character development

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.959
from her counterpart big mobster characters
from The Dark Knight Trilogy.

00:03:58.959 --> 00:04:01.752
I’ll give her a chance, since she’s one
of the bigger actors on the show we should

00:04:01.752 --> 00:04:02.752
expect to see a lot of her in season 1.

00:04:02.752 --> 00:04:06.329
But the majority of this first episode focuses
on Oswald Cobblepot, which made me really

00:04:06.329 --> 00:04:07.329
happy.

00:04:07.329 --> 00:04:09.959
The penguin is definitely one of my favorite
batman villains and his character arc is a

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:12.930
lot like that of the city itself.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:18.269
Gotham City slowly descends into madness,
Cobblepot slowly descends into madness.

00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:25.860
Until eventually he takes on the Penguin persona.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:34.110
The interesting thing they’ve already teased
about season 1 is that they’re bringing

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:39.060
on Hugo Strange and developing Arkham Asylum
as a new big location.

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:45.310
Gotham is a Batman origin story and it’s
an Arkham Asylum origin story.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.550
Arkham will be the mystery briefcase of pain
that the writers reach into to pull out Batman

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:50.740
villains for the show.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:55.199
If you never heard it, Joss Whedon had this
big story about the briefcase of pain.

00:04:55.199 --> 00:05:00.240
He said on the set of Thor The Dark World
he asked Anthony Hopkins about some of his

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.960
inspiration for characters and Hopkins said
he keeps a tiny mental briefcase where he

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.830
stores painful things.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:13.120
And when he needs a character to go crazy
he just reaches into the briefcase and pulls

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:14.430
out something.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.440
So Arkham Asylum will be Gotham’s tiny briefcase
of pain.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:23.810
In terms of villains the first episode mostly
focuses on The Penguin, but it does introduce

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:29.610
The Riddler, Catwoman and Poison Ivy.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.530
The show treats them in this very precog way,
like you know what their future is and it’s

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.360
the job of the series to show you how it all
unfolds.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.220
The Riddler is one of the bigger characters
I’m really looking forward to seeing more

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:42.460
of, he doesn’t have a big part in the premiere,
but his role inside the show.

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:46.280
His day job puts him right next to Gordon
and Bullock.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.500
On the other side of the fence, young Bruce
Wayne and Alfred.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.720
They don’t have as much screentime in the
first episode as they will later but the story

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.140
sets up the triggers for the cowl.

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:58.759
David Mazouz, who plays young bruce wayne
does a really good job and I’m interested

00:05:58.759 --> 00:06:01.120
to see how often the show visits his character.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:06.550
He’s not the main character of the series,
but he’s one of the most important ones.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:07.599
He might be short, he’s a little kid.

00:06:07.599 --> 00:06:09.599
But he does cast a very long shadow.

00:06:09.599 --> 00:06:14.070
I actually found myself staring at the shadows
whenever he was on screen to see if they used

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:15.070
any digital effects for cape and cowl easter
eggs.

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:18.139
Alfred is played by sean pertwee from the
musketeers.

00:06:18.139 --> 00:06:22.259
If you watch my doctor who videos you’ll
also know him as the son of the Third Doctor

00:06:22.259 --> 00:06:23.919
Jon Pertwee.

00:06:23.919 --> 00:06:29.509
They play up a bit more of Alfred’s history
in the British Military.

00:06:29.509 --> 00:06:37.000
Pertwee is a much bigger Alfred than the Gandalf
version of the character Michael Caine played.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.919
So I’m expecting to see Alfred get in a
couple fist fights this year.

00:06:39.919 --> 00:06:40.919
Look forward to that.

00:06:40.919 --> 00:06:43.310
It would be very cool to see Alfred teach
a young Bruce Wayne to fight off bullies.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:47.539
The other young members of the cast, Catwoman
and Poison Ivy are also only briefly seen

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:49.979
in the episode but that’s just because of
the time limitations.

00:06:49.979 --> 00:06:52.370
We’ll see a lot more of them in future episodes.

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:56.560
They tease a really interesting relationship
developing between Bruce Wayne and Selina

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.729
Kyle so I’m interested to see where the
show takes it.

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:05.639
Generally, what I think the show proves is
that Gotham City can be interesting even without

00:07:05.639 --> 00:07:06.639
a fully actualized Batman.

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:11.039
I was really happy that the show didn’t
present the absence of Batman as a big thing.

00:07:11.039 --> 00:07:13.720
It doesn’t try to be too self aware about
what’s NOT there.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:18.210
So you don’t walk away feeling like something’s
missing.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:29.969
Officially Right now, Fox has already ordered
a full season.

00:07:29.969 --> 00:07:35.479
So they’ll probably break it into 8 or 10
episodes this fall, then the rest in January

00:07:35.479 --> 00:07:36.479
or February.

00:07:36.479 --> 00:07:40.060
So it’s not like we have to worry about
it getting cancelled.

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.819
They are shooting all 16 of those episodes.

00:07:43.819 --> 00:07:48.350
They’ve still got several to finish.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:51.930
As I start doing videos from the episodes,
I’ll be sure to include stuff from behind

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.470
the scenes as they continue to finish filming.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:54.590
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:08:01.229
But generally you can expect several more
new batman villains to show up before the

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:02.870
finale.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:12.199
We won’t know about season 2 until after
the first several episodes, so don’t worry

00:08:12.199 --> 00:08:13.199
about that yet.

00:08:13.199 --> 00:08:14.800
I will be doing videos all season.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.909
I was really happy that I stuck with Agents
of SHIELD for all of season 1.

00:08:17.909 --> 00:08:23.189
A lot of people dumped that show before it
got good, it took it about half a season to

00:08:23.189 --> 00:08:25.819
get there, but I’m also really excited for
that to come back.

00:08:25.819 --> 00:08:30.229
I’m working on a season 2 preview video
for that to post tonight.

00:08:30.229 --> 00:08:33.159
Next week during the premiere what I’ll
do is a top 10 video, since this is already

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:34.159
kind of my review.

00:08:34.159 --> 00:08:35.525
I’ll also be live-tweeting, without being
super spoilery of course, but if you want

00:08:35.525 --> 00:08:39.640
to play along with me, my twitter and facebook
links are in the description.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:43.620
Right now you can click here to learn more
about some of the villains coming to Gotham

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.720
and you can click here to start getting ready
for Arrow and The Flash.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:47.960
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

